From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: drop the netgen-occt runtime dependency

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [netgen-occt ships no riscv64 wheel; OCCT is built from source and linked statically instead]

netgen-mesher's wheel normally depends on the separately published
netgen-occt wheel for the OpenCASCADE shared libraries it dynamically
loads at run time. netgen-occt has no riscv64 build on PyPI, so the
riscv64 workflow builds the same OCCT 7.8.1 release from source
(BUILD_LIBRARY_TYPE=Static) and links it straight into netgen's own
extension modules, with no runtime library left to depend on.

---
 pyproject.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -14,7 +14,6 @@
 license = "LGPL-2.1-only"
 requires-python = ">=3.10"
 dependencies = [
-    "netgen-occt==7.8.1",
     "numpy",
 ]

--
2.43.0
